course: dictionary
lesson: 8914
title: Sickle: a tool and a shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sickle is a farm tool with a short handle and a curved, C-shaped blade. People used it to cut grass, grain or corn by hand. «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, doing work that once took dozens of people with sickles.» The word sickles shows that people did this job by hand, with a tool like this, before machines.
explain: The word can also describe a shape. Anything shaped like the blade is sickle-shaped. «In spring, Leo the lion appears in the south, its head and mane a backwards question mark called the Sickle.» The star pattern is curved like the blade, so it is named after the tool. Look for the shape in the words around the word: curved, C-shaped, question mark.
fact: A sickle has a short handle and a curved blade.
fact: A sickle is used to cut grass, grain or corn by hand.
fact: A sickle moon is a thin, curved moon, shaped like the blade.
fact: Sickle cell disease is an illness in which red blood cells bend into a sickle shape.
fact: A scythe is a larger tool with a long handle, so it is not the same as a sickle.
exercise: «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, doing work that once took dozens of people with sickles.» Which tool did people use by hand to cut wheat before machines like this? | Telescopes | Trumpets | Kites | *Sickles
exercise: «In spring, Leo the lion appears in the south, its head and mane a backwards question mark called the Sickle.» What does the Sickle mean here? | A large farm animal | A kind of cloud | *A star pattern shaped like a curved blade | A type of sandwich
exercise: Which tool is a sickle? | A long-handled tool with a straight blade | A bucket on a rope | *A short-handled tool with a curved, C-shaped blade | A tool with wheels that drives across fields
test: On a clear night the sky showed a sickle moon, thin and curved. What is a sickle moon? | *A thin, curved moon, like a sickle blade | A moon that is very bright and round | A full, round moon | A moon hidden by clouds
test: Which word means shaped like a sickle? | Round | Straight | Heavy | *Sickle-shaped
exam: «The hammer and sickle» stood for workers and farmers on an old flag. Why was a sickle on that flag? | Because sickles were used to build houses | *Because farmers used sickles to harvest crops by hand | Because the flag was made in a shop that sold sickles | Because a sickle is a kind of flower
